{"member_key":"rs-2657","house":"Rajya Sabha","kind":"special_mentions","records":[{"title":"Demand for development of tourism infrastructure in the Union Territory of Jammu & Kashmir.","date":"2026-08-12","details":[["Date","12/08/2026"],["Session","271"],["Ministry","TOURISM"],["Statement","Shri Sat Paul Sharma: \r\nI seek to raise a matter of urgent public importance\r\nregarding the development of tourism infrastructure in the Union Territory of\r\nJammu & Kashmir. The Government of India has launched flagship initiatives\r\nsuch as Swadesh Darshan 2.0 and the PRASHAD (Pilgrimage Rejuvenation and\r\nSpiritual, Heritage Augmentation Drive) Scheme to develop world-class\r\nsustainable tourism and pilgrimage infrastructure. While these schemes have\r\ncreated opportunities for tourism development, several destinations in Jammu\r\nProvince with immense religious, heritage, eco-tourism and adventure tourism potential\r\ncontinue to require substantial infrastructure support. I, therefore,\r\nurge the Government to:\n1. Prepare and\r\nimplement a comprehensive tourism infrastructure plan for Jammu Province under\r\nSwadesh Darshan 2.0 and PRASHAD by including eligible destinations such as Shiv\r\nKhori, Patnitop, Sanasar, Poonch ,Bhaderwah, Basohli, Mansar, Surinsar, and\r\nother high-potential tourist destinations. 2. \r\nConduct an independent audit of all projects sanctioned and executed in Jammu\r\n& Kashmir under Swadesh Darshan and PRASHAD, including details of funds\r\nsanctioned, expenditure incurred, physical progress, quality of works,\r\ntimelines and the tourism outcomes achieved. Strengthening tourism\r\ninfrastructure in Jammu Province will boost employment, encourage private\r\ninvestment, increase tourist footfall, and contribute significantly to the\r\neconomic development of the Union Territory while ensuring transparency and\r\naccountability in the implementation of Central Government schemes.\n(ENDS)"],["Reply","No Reply"]],"links":[{"label":"Official source","url":"https://rsdoc.nic.in/memberGetdata/Get_SpecialMentionmemberwise?mpcode=2657"}]},{"title":"Demand for extending special Central financial assistance for flood affected areas of Jammu & Kashmir.","date":"2026-08-05","details":[["Date","05/08/2026"],["Session","271"],["Ministry","HOME AFFAIRS"],["Statement","Shri Sat Paul Sharma:???? \r\nI seek to draw attention of the Government to the recurring flash floods,\r\ncloudbursts, landslides and other natural calamities that have caused\r\nwidespread devastation across Jammu & Kashmir, including the recent tragedy\r\nin Rajouri-Poonch and other Districts of J&K UT. These disasters have\r\nresulted in loss of precious lives, destruction of homes, damage to public\r\ninfrastructure and severe disruption to the livelihoods of thousands of\r\nfamilies. While immediate rescue and relief efforts are undertaken, the\r\naffected families often face prolonged hardship due to inadequate resources for\r\nreconstruction and rehabilitation.\nI, therefore, urge the Government to consider extending special Central\r\nfinancial assistance to Jammu & Kashmir for the rehabilitation and\r\nreconstruction of houses, restoration of damaged public infrastructure, revival\r\nof livelihoods, and support to the affected. I also request the Government to\r\nconsider a special rehabilitation package for families who have lost their\r\nhomes or earning members in such calamities, so that they can rebuild their\r\nlives with dignity. Given the increasing frequency and intensity of such\r\ndisasters in the hilly region, a sustained and adequately funded Central rehabilitation\r\nmechanism is essential to ensure timely recovery and long-term resilience in\r\nJammu & Kashmir.\n (ENDS)"],["Reply","No Reply"]],"links":[{"label":"Official source","url":"https://rsdoc.nic.in/memberGetdata/Get_SpecialMentionmemberwise?mpcode=2657"}]},{"title":"Concern over growing menace of narco-terrorism and drug abuse in Jammu and Kashmir.","date":"2026-